Replaces: gnome-system-monitor
Description: GNOME System Monitor with the MaluOS tabs (GPUs, MaluOS Network, Queue)
 GNOME's process viewer and system resource monitor (Processes, Resources, File
 Systems), carried by MaluOS with its own tabs: GPUs (this computer's GPUs, the
 switch that shares them with the MaluOS network, the models loaded and the
 queue; the network's GPUs once the desk is enrolled), MaluOS Network (this
 node as the gateway's node API reports it, the nodes it is paired with, the
 office) and Queue (every lane and every call of the gateway's queue, with
 pause, resume, cancel and a call's class). The tabs render what the MaluOS
 session service publishes and compute nothing themselves; they appear only
 when that service answers, so on a plain GNOME desktop this is System Monitor
 as upstream ships it. Replaces Ubuntu's gnome-system-monitor package (same
 application id, same files).
